          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℬ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \;\colon\; \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{B}
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            we say that it
            %em
              has
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiscrete+object"} codiscrete object
            if it has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi coDisc
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} coDisc \,\colon\, \mathcal{B} \hookrightarrow \mathcal{E}
          %p
            This is for instance the case for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+topos"} local topos
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Disc
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi coDisc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Disc \dashv \Gamma \dashv coDisc) \;\colon\; \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{B}
          %p
            In this situation, we say that a
            %strong concrete object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{E}
            is one for which the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi coDisc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Gamma \dashv coDisc)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit of an adjunction
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+sheaf"} concrete sheaf
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            then this is called a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf"} concrete (∞,1)-sheaf
            or the like.
          %p
            The dual notion is that of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-concrete+object"} co-concrete object
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful functor
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
            is concrete.
          %h3#concretification_factorization Concretification factorization
          #ConcretificationFactorization.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+topos"} local topos
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
